{"id":395,"date":"2020-09-22T14:39:40","date_gmt":"2020-09-22T14:39:40","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/?page_id=395"},"modified":"2025-11-11T16:21:17","modified_gmt":"2025-11-11T16:21:17","slug":"meet-the-tutors","status":"publish","type":"page","link":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/meet-the-tutors\/","title":{"rendered":"Meet the Tutors"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover is-light has-custom-content-position is-position-bottom-left pad-5 page-banner\" style=\"min-height:600px\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-background-dim-30 has-background-dim\" style=\"background-color:#161228\"><\/span><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"2560\" height=\"1707\" class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-11965\" alt=\"\" src=\"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2025\/01\/IMG_4791-scaled.jpg\" data-object-fit=\"cover\" srcset=\"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2025\/01\/IMG_4791-scaled.jpg 2560w, https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2025\/01\/IMG_4791-300x200.jpg 300w, https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2025\/01\/IMG_4791-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2025\/01\/IMG_4791-768x512.jpg 768w, https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2025\/01\/IMG_4791-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2025\/01\/IMG_4791-2048x1365.jpg 2048w, https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2025\/01\/IMG_4791-18x12.jpg 18w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 2560px) 100vw, 2560px\" \/><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\">\n<h1 class=\"has-white-color has-text-color\">Meet the Tutors<\/h1>\n<\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"is-layout-flow wp-block-group pad-5\"><div class=\"wp-block-group__inner-container\">\n<p>Tutoring at AIMS centres is a wonderful opportunity to meet and work closely with highly-respected scientists from around the world, as well as brilliant and highly motivated students from across Africa. Students coming to AIMS have strong backgrounds in the mathematical sciences (including pure and applied mathematics, computer science, mathematical biology and other fields).<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>While outstanding visiting lecturers are recruited from all over the world to teach and prepare students for advanced postgraduate research, the courses are unusually broad in scope and employ the latest pedagogical methods in order to stimulate critical and creative thinking.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>To facilitate student participation and follow-up, each Centre offers a Tutoring Fellowship which permits post-doc and doctorate researchers to work as dedicated teaching assistants, with the responsibility of providing capacity building for the students 24\/7. The unique residential character of the institute allows for optimum interaction between students and tutors.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Meet our Tutors for the 2025\/2026 academic year.<\/p>\n<\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"is-layout-flow wp-block-group pad-5-no-top\"><div class=\"wp-block-group__inner-container\">\n<div class=\"row w-00\">        \n\n        <div class=\"col-md-4 col-lg-3 no-class-spacer\"> \n\n<div class=\"profile-card-img img-bg\" style=\"background-image:url('https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2025\/11\/Dr.-Carole-Madengko-Simo-Cameroon.png')\">\n\n\n\n\n\n <\/div>\n<div class=\"profile-card-bottom bg-primary   center-text\"> \n\n<div class=\"profile-card-name pad-5 white-text sans-serif-bold\"> <strong> <p>Dr. Carole Madengko Simo <\/strong><\/p>\n<p> Cameroon <\/p>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n\n        \n\n        <div class=\"col-md-4 col-lg-3 no-class-spacer\"> \n\n<div class=\"profile-card-img img-bg\" style=\"background-image:url('https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2025\/11\/Dr.-Joseph-Owuor-Owino.png')\">\n\n\n\n\n\n <\/div>\n<div class=\"profile-card-bottom bg-primary   center-text\"> \n\n<div class=\"profile-card-name pad-5 white-text sans-serif-bold\"> <strong> <p>Dr. Joseph Owuor Owino <\/strong><\/p>\n<p> Kenya <\/p>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n\n        \n\n        <div class=\"col-md-4 col-lg-3 no-class-spacer\"> \n\n<div class=\"profile-card-img img-bg\" style=\"background-image:url('https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2025\/11\/Dr.-Mubarak-Muhammed.png')\">\n\n\n\n\n\n <\/div>\n<div class=\"profile-card-bottom bg-primary   center-text\"> \n\n<div class=\"profile-card-name pad-5 white-text sans-serif-bold\"> <strong> <p>Dr. Mubarak Muhammed <\/strong><\/p>\n<p> Nigeria <\/p>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n\n        \n\n        <div class=\"col-md-4 col-lg-3 no-class-spacer\"> \n\n<div class=\"profile-card-img img-bg\" style=\"background-image:url('https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2025\/11\/Elizabeth-Dadzie.png')\">\n\n\n\n\n\n <\/div>\n<div class=\"profile-card-bottom bg-primary   center-text\"> \n\n<div class=\"profile-card-name pad-5 white-text sans-serif-bold\"> <strong> <p>Elizabeth Dadzie <\/strong><\/p>\n<p> Ghana  <\/p>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n\n    \n<\/div><\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<p><\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Tutoring at AIMS centres is a wonderful opportunity to meet and work closely with highly-respected scientists from around the world, as well as brilliant and highly motivated students from across Africa. Students coming to AIMS have strong backgrounds in the mathematical sciences (including pure and applied mathematics, computer science, mathematical biology and other fields). While<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":0,"parent":0,"menu_order":0,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","template":"","meta":{"advgb_blocks_editor_width":"","advgb_blocks_columns_visual_guide":""},"acf":[],"coauthors":[],"author_meta":{"author_link":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/author\/chris\/","display_name":"chris"},"relative_dates":{"cre